{"id":"amen","title":"'Amen, amen, I say to you'","kind":"phrase","en":["Amen,? (?:amen,? )?I say"],"la":["Amen,? (?:amen,? )?dico"],"gist":"'Amen' means 'so be it' or 'truly', and in Jewish speech it comes at the end of what someone else has said. Jesus does something unheard of: he begins his own sayings with it. John doubles it. It marks the words as weighty and spoken on his own authority.","original":"Hebrew amen (from a root meaning 'firm, reliable'); Greek amen.","passages":[{"ref":"Matthew 5:18","note":"'Amen I say to you, till heaven and earth pass...'"},{"ref":"John 3:3","note":"'Amen, amen I say to thee...'"},{"ref":"John 6:47","note":"Before the bread of life discourse."}],"related":["i-am"],"total":75,"byBook":{"JHN":25,"LUK":7,"MAT":30,"MRK":13},"verses":["JHN.1.51","JHN.3.3","JHN.3.5","JHN.3.11","JHN.5.19","JHN.5.24","JHN.5.25","JHN.6.26","JHN.6.32","JHN.6.47","JHN.6.54","JHN.8.34","JHN.8.51","JHN.8.58","JHN.10.1","JHN.10.7","JHN.12.24","JHN.13.16","JHN.13.20","JHN.13.21","JHN.13.38","JHN.14.12","JHN.16.20","JHN.16.23","JHN.21.18","LUK.4.24","LUK.7.9","LUK.12.37","LUK.18.17","LUK.18.29","LUK.21.32","LUK.23.43","MAT.5.18","MAT.5.26","MAT.6.2","MAT.6.5","MAT.6.16","MAT.8.10","MAT.10.15","MAT.10.23","MAT.10.42","MAT.11.11","MAT.13.17","MAT.16.28","MAT.17.19","MAT.18.3","MAT.18.13","MAT.18.18","MAT.19.23","MAT.19.28","MAT.21.21","MAT.21.31","MAT.23.36","MAT.24.2","MAT.24.34","MAT.24.47","MAT.25.12","MAT.25.40","MAT.25.45","MAT.26.13","MAT.26.21","MAT.26.34","MRK.3.28","MRK.8.12","MRK.8.39","MRK.9.40","MRK.10.15","MRK.10.29","MRK.11.23","MRK.12.43","MRK.13.30","MRK.14.9","MRK.14.18","MRK.14.25","MRK.14.30"]}